Limit: the plain not-found set (no audit row) is a 404, a bare {status: NEVER_FOUND}, and a well-formed v1 body with status PENDING or NEVER_FOUND; that is taken from the repository's Gateway fixtures, not from Hermes' own code
Warn: the Hermes receipt port now reports why a receipt was not read (kind HTTP_STATUS, CONTENT_TYPE, TOO_LARGE, TIMEOUT, TRANSPORT, PARSE or SCHEMA with the first failing check) and the sweep records CANONICAL_TURN_RECEIPT_LOOKUP_FAILED once per turn per cause while the turn stays IN_DOUBT; nothing settles on a malformed receipt and the parser accepts exactly what it accepted before
Warn: a lookup error does not count in reconcileUnresolved's failed total, because the daemon throws and backs off whenever failed is above zero; an unexpected throw from a port now does count
